  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the coordinates of the point on $y=\\ln x$ where the tangent has gradient $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nThen find the equation of the tangent and normal there, in the form $y=mx+b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Point: $(2,\\ln 2)$.\n\nTangent: $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-1+\\ln 2$.\n\nNormal: $y=-2x+4+\\ln 2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{1}{x}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}&=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\x&=2\\\\y&=\\ln 2\\end{align*}$$\nThe point is $(2,\\ln 2)$.\n\nTangent:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-\\ln 2&=\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{2}x-1+\\ln 2\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal has gradient $-2$, the negative reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-\\ln 2&=-2(x-2)\\\\y&=-2x+4+\\ln 2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
